# Confidentiality mapping and banned-terms list.
# Committing this undoes every sanitization decision in the repository.
private/

# NOTE (ADR-002, 2026-08-19): resources/diagrams/*.svg used to be ignored here on the
# assumption it was always regenerated from .mmd at build time. That assumption is gone —
# ADR-002 commits to a one-time render (TASK 17) with the .svg as real, checked-in content;
# the build only ever copies it. Do not re-add an ignore pattern for resources/diagrams/*.svg
# without updating ADR-002 first.
# resources/diagrams/*.png stays ignored below (TASK 1: original, unsanitized vendor PNGs
# for the attendance diagrams existed transiently during the redraw — unrelated to this note).
resources/diagrams/*.png

# Local scratch space — never published content, never a build input.
tmp/

# Original unsanitized source material
*.original.*
uploads/

# Working intake notes — raw answers about availability, job search, and
# employment specifics, not for publication. Not a pattern: only this file.
resources/site/intake.md

.DS_Store
node_modules/

# Design canvas build intermediates (TASK 8). `.fonts/` is a cache of public OFL
# webfont files, re-downloaded by build.mjs; `build/` is the fonts-expanded copy of
# `src/*.dc.html` that seed-canvas.mjs consumes — both regenerate from `src/` on demand.
# `src/` (the authored .dc.html/canvas.json) is real content and stays tracked.
docs/design/canvas/.fonts/
docs/design/canvas/build/

# Runtime trace. Machine-written operational output, not knowledge: it would dirty
# every diff, and this repository may yet be published. The schema is documented in
# docs/harness/evidence.md, which IS committed.
evidence/

# the site build
site/node_modules/
site/dist/
site/.astro/

# Wrangler's local state (TASK 32). `state/` is the local simulation of bindings that
# `wrangler dev` persists between runs; `tmp/` is its scratch. Machine-written, regenerated
# on demand, and never a build input — the same category as site/.astro/ directly above.
# check-site's own exclusion list already carried `.wrangler`; this is the git half.
site/.wrangler/

# The mutation gate's working trees (TASK 15). `.stryker-tmp/` is the sandbox Stryker copies
# the project into and mutates; `reports/` is its HTML report. Both are machine-written
# operational output, regenerated by every run — the same category as evidence/, and for the
# same stated reason: they would dirty every diff and they are not knowledge.
.stryker-tmp/
reports/

# The smoke tier's working output (TASK 41). `test-results/` holds per-failure traces,
# screenshots and error context; `playwright-report/` is the HTML reporter's output. Both
# are machine-written and regenerated by every run — same category as reports/ above, and
# both appear only when a run fails, which is exactly when nobody wants a dirty diff.
site/test-results/
site/playwright-report/

# The smoke tier's screenshot deliverable (TASK 51): PNGs captured at the three sanctioned
# widths in both themes, for a human to look at — not a diffing artifact, and not authored
# content. Machine-written and regenerated by every run of screenshots.smoke.spec.ts, whose
# SCREENSHOTS_DIR constant is the one place this path is declared.
site/screenshots/
